        "title": "Historiography - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Historiography has two related but distinct meanings: (1) the history of historical writing — who wrote what, when, and why; (2) the theory and methodology of how history should be written — what standards of evidence, explanation, and narrative are legitimate. The field is simultaneously a catalog of past historians and a live debate about the epistemological foundations of the discipline."
